From 0d10aeda925cc1a7f70b42edf5d777e8d4e66d33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:08:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 193/213] fix: the ray traced hit gets the material's gloss
 map, not just its scalar

CE ships _ddna as BC5U, DXTDecompress sets sourceChannels = 2 for it and
DXTDecompressRow writes a literal 255 into alpha, so the atlas normal slice's
alpha was a constant 1.0 for every material in the level and the hit's
smoothness collapsed to the material scalar - flat across every texel, while
the same surface seen directly is modulated per texel (report 02d section 3).

CE's gloss is a separate texture: Illum.cfx GetSurfaceAttributes computes
    attribs.Smoothness = MatSpecColor.w * GetSmoothnessTex(smoothnessTex, tc)
and GetSmoothnessTex returns the map's .r - a multiply, not a replace, and
Terrain.cfx and Vegetation.cfx use the identical product. The consumer already
forms matInfo1.z * saturate(vNor.w) with matInfo1.z = MatSpecColor.w, so only
vNor.w was missing a real value.

CheckStoreTextureInPool's EFTT_NORMALS branch now fetches the material's
EFTT_SMOOTHNESS low-res copy through the same GetLowResSystemCopy path and size
snapping as every other layer and writes its red channel into the slice's alpha,
nearest-resampled by the new RT_ResampleIndex when the two copies snapped to
different sizes. With no gloss map the alpha stays 255, so the result degrades
to the scalar, i.e. to exactly the previous picture. No record change, no extra
atlas slice, no shader change.

e_svoTI_RT_SelfTest gains a gloss resample check (4 size pairs: in range,
monotonic, and the last destination texel maps to the last source texel when the
source is not finer than the destination) and the verdict now requires it.
e_svoTI_RT_Debug's help string spells out mode 0, the magenta markers of modes 5
and 10, and that mode 11 is no longer flat per material.

Known: the atlas dedupe key is the normal texture, so two materials sharing one
normal map but not one gloss map share the first one's gloss, and a material
with a gloss map but no normal map still gets the scalar. Route 2 of report 02d
(a fifth atlas layer) is the escape hatch if either shows up.

